 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids. January to February came in under 90% of normal in 35 of those years, more than any other pair. In 2025 November to December reached just 45% of normal, and in 2026 so far February to March and March to April both sit at 44%. Every grid had its driest year in 2016, with grid 17887 lowest at 61%.</p>"}
